moglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\nHome\nResearch & Innovation\nGrants\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\nLeft Sidebar\n2 min read · May 6, 2025\nMay 6, 2025\nShare\nGrants\nEHA Research Grants\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nThe EHA Advanced Research Grant is a type of EHA Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years.\nEligibility\nYou’re eligible if:\nYou’re an EHA member\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\nPurely clinical research projects\nProjects in health economics\nOther non-lab-based research\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\nSpecific criteria for the EHA Advanced Research Grant\nOur Advanced Research Grant is suitable for researchers who:\nAre currently carrying out basic or translational lab-based research in hematology\nReceived a PhD or PharmD less than eight years before the closing date listed above\nHave at least one first author publication\nIf you received your PhD or PharmD outside of this timeframe, please check our policy on life events. If this policy applies to you, you can ask us to extend the period of eligibility.\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Advanced Research Grant’ on your application form.\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in countries less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. ​You can see a full list of these countries on our page about extending the reach of EHA Research Grants. Applicants, who received their PhD or PharmD more than eight years before the closing date, are also eligible.\nIf you have questions about your eligibility, you can contact us at [email protected] before submitting an application.\nHow to apply for an EHA Research Grant\nWhat an EHA Research Grant covers\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\nShare\nGrants\nEHA Research Grants\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\nMission and vision\nJobs\nSponsor EHA\nContact us\nFollow us\nPrivacy statement\nTerms and conditions\nSubscribe\nCopyright © 2026\nBecome an EHA Mentor\nEHA Mentorship Program\nDiscover the rewards of mentoring\nApply by October 29\nApply today",
